sm64-saturn-port build-time patch: libyaul kernel TLSF private pool 0xA000 -> 0x4000
====================================================================================

Sprint 2 Task T2.2 (plan: docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-15-sprint2-cadence-recovery.md).

WHAT
  Shrinks libyaul's kernel-internal TLSF `_private_pool` from 40,960 to
  16,384 bytes (-24,576 B of HWRAM .bss), and carries the MALLOC_IMPL_TLSF
  configuration macro into the translation unit (the port compiles this file
  outside libyaul's env.mk, which is where -DMALLOC_IMPL_TLSF normally comes
  from; .yaul.env pins YAUL_OPTION_MALLOC_IMPL=tlsf).

WHY THE SIZE IS SAFE (measured, not assumed)
  T2.1's instrumented capture (docs/saturn/evidence/reports/
  sprint2-t2_1-peak-capture.md, Peak 2) walked the live pool's physical TLSF
  chain and stain-scanned the boot-zeroed pool over a 24,000-frame scripted
  route: historical extent 8,276 bytes from pool base (TLSF control 3,188 B +
  six boot-time blocks totalling 4,980 B payload; zero churn after boot).
  A 0x4000 pool provides 13,188 B of arena after control+sentinel:
  8,108 B of margin over the measured extent.

HOW IT IS APPLIED (never in-place)
  third_party/libyaul is a READ-ONLY pinned submodule
  (6012f79f237773378c8014e70d8998ad95a38d98). The sourceboot Makefile's
  `sourceboot-libyaul-mm-patch` staging rule extracts the pristine file
  bytes from the pinned submodule commit with `git show` (canonical LF,
  independent of checkout smudge), verifies both the submodule HEAD and the
  pristine file SHA-256, applies this patch with GNU patch into
  $(SOURCEBOOT_GENERATED)/libyaul_mm_internal.c, verifies the patched
  SHA-256, and compiles that staged copy as an ordinary port object.
  Because the object precedes `-lyaul` on the link line and defines every
  global symbol of the archive's mm/internal.o member, the linker never
  pulls the upstream member (same supersede mechanism as the soft-fp
  archive; see the LINK ORDER note in src/port/saturn/sourceboot/Makefile).
  kernel/internal.h (not installed by yaul) is staged verbatim next to it.

